From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 01:19:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] taskschd: let scripts drive the objects, and keep what
 Windows 10 added to a task.

Each object's IDispatch speaks for its interface through the type
library, the most derived one as on Windows, and the collections give
out enumerators, so a script can create and walk a task as it would
there.

A definition keeps ITaskSettings3's maintenance settings and volatility,
IPrincipal2's token SID type and required privileges, IExecAction2's
hidden window, the COM handler, email and message actions, and the
registration info's security descriptor.  Each setter of something a
later schema added raises the compatibility the definition shares with
all it holds, as Windows does, and the XML carries what that version
has: writing omits the rest, reading refuses it where the document
declares an earlier version, and checks what each action needs.

The XML of the registration info, the settings or the actions on their
own is not implemented on Windows either.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit ff3d5e46bce9c24bfa1199ffd37d1cee8eeaf75a)

